# Cloudflare Pages headers — the replacement for the Cache-Control rules the
# deploy workflow wrote into Hostinger's .htaccess (and the separate
# _astro/.htaccess). Apache config does not travel with the site.
#
# Getting this wrong is not theoretical: before those rules existed, Hostinger
# served HTML with no Cache-Control at all, browsers fell back to heuristic
# caching, and a deploy stayed invisible for over a day. See CLAUDE.md.

# Everything revalidates by default. max-age=0 + must-revalidate still allows
# caching — the browser just has to ask first, and gets a cheap 304 when
# nothing changed. This deliberately covers HTML, images and the PDFs: none of
# them are content-hashed, so a stale copy is a real bug.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Astro's build output is content-hashed — the filename changes whenever the
# bytes do — so these can be cached permanently.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
